{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts","id":471285,"title":"On the innovative use of Elemental Gifts...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-07T09:00:00-07:00","id":471285,"title":"On the innovative use of Elemental Gifts...","content":"Ok, some questions are already popping in my Werewolf Chronicle, and I need some help. I have a pretty deviant little shaman in my group with Elemental Gifts.<br /> <br /> 1. Can the &quot;Influence Air&quot; via Elemental Gifts be used to drain air out of opponents lungs, and what would be a counter roll? Stamina?<br /> 1a. Can &quot;Influence Air&quot; also be used to create a strong wind so you don't get hurt falling down?<br /> 2. Can &quot;Influence Water&quot; be used to remove water from a human body? For instance summon all that water in a form of a ball floating above you?<br /> 3. What roll should be used for summoning a giant hand made out of rock to hold an opponent using &quot;Influence Earth&quot;, and what would be a proper counter roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T09:26:56-07:00","id":471334,"title":"","content":"For the Influence Air questions I'd say yes, though I'd have to think about a Defense roll for a while. Probably Stamina, since that's the attribute for holding one's breath.<br /> <br /> For the Influence Water one I'd say sure. Probably not all of it, as a lot of the 'water' is mixed with other things making it something other than water. But you'd probably do bashing damage to represent desiccation.<br /> <br /> I think the dicepool for that Influence Earth one would be the same as any Influence Earth roll. Strength + Survival + Honor. Though I'd be tempted to allow a specialization for Brawl or Grapple to help out. Countering it would probably involve Defense or Dodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T09:30:28-07:00","id":471337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts#post471285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Can the &quot;Influence Air&quot; via Elemental Gifts be used to drain air out of opponents lungs, and what would be a counter roll? Stamina?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends how many dots of influence the character has. At one fot, you can only Manipulate your area of influence, making minor changes to its nature - the temperature of the air, the wind speed and direction, maybe the humidity, etc. So I'd say no, you can't forcibly add or remove air from an area. At two dots, you can Strengthen, so you might be able to make the air thicker, but certainly not thinner. At three dots you can Control, and yes, I would allow that to force the air out of someone's lungs. Maybe make it a contested roll against the target's Resolve + Stamina, and the target can't breathe for a number of turns equal to the attacker's successes, then use the normal rules for suffocation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts#post471285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1a. Can &quot;Influence Air&quot; also be used to create a strong wind so you don't get hurt falling down?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow that at one or two dots. Decrease the falling damage by the number of successes on the Influence roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts#post471285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Can &quot;Influence Water&quot; be used to remove water from a human body? For instance summon all that water in a form of a ball floating above you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I would not allow that one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts#post471285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. What roll should be used for summoning a giant hand made out of rock to hold an opponent using &quot;Influence Earth&quot;, and what would be a proper counter roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Elemental gift facets all list what the dice pool for using their respective influence is. For Flesh of Earth, it's Strength + Survival + Honor. Since you're grabbing the target, they would contest the roll with Strength + Brawl and whoever got the most successes could perform one of the grapple maneuvers, as per the normal grappling rules. (Obviously, any maneuvers the target performs will be taken against the stone hand).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-07-2015, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T09:36:03-07:00","id":471339,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the answers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T09:46:16-07:00","id":471343,"title":"","content":"On #2 I think that I'd rule that water inside of a living being isn't 'water', it's part of that being and outside of the Influence of the water purview. It's simpler that way and more thematic for the general Werewolf game favoring the metaphorical over the literal. That said doing the water sucking thing as a narrative from of the Blast Numina would be perfectly fine with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T11:17:49-07:00","id":471387,"title":"","content":"For the Earth one? I'd penalize the roll by the opponent's defense, if the user is successful he achieves a grapple with strength equal to his influence dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T11:23:41-07:00","id":471390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=471387#post471387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Earth one? I'd penalize the roll by the opponent's defense, if the user is successful he achieves a grapple with strength equal to his influence dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right, I forgot the initial roll to initiate a grapple was resisted by Defense. I would still roll the Influence dice pool for the grapple roll though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T13:33:56-07:00","id":471611,"title":"","content":"Charlequin has the right of it, though they have a slight mix-up; one dot is <i>Strengthen</i>, while two dots is <i>Manipulate</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T14:06:05-07:00","id":471669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=471611#post471611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlequin has the right of it, though they have a slight mix-up; one dot is <i>Strengthen</i>, while two dots is <i>Manipulate</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's right. Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T14:28:36-07:00","id":471689,"title":"","content":"I'm honestly still a little fuzzy about where the line between manipulate and control is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T14:39:03-07:00","id":471699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=471689#post471689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly still a little fuzzy about where the line between manipulate and control is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manipulate lets you change qualities of the thing you're influencing without changing the thing itself. So if you're using Influence: Fire to manipulate a candle flame, you can make it flicker, burn hotter or colder, change color, that kind of thing. But you can't make it float independent of the candle, or engulf a larger area. With Control you become Pyro from X-Men, and with Create you become a fire bender from Avatar.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, the distinction is kind of subjective, but does that make a bit more sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T14:51:21-07:00","id":471720,"title":"","content":"Kinda. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T20:24:23-07:00","id":472017,"title":"","content":"So go out and kill yourself an Earth Queen.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/C0xbBG8NzcE\" data-code=\"C0xbBG8NzcE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/C0xbBG8NzcE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T22:13:49-07:00","id":472201,"title":"","content":"Just one more renown and you can do it the other way around. Pump them full of air until they're like Thunder in Big Trouble Little China. The other elements would be no less effective, created and shoved into a person. Or just created inside their stomach and lungs.<br /> <br /> As horrible imagery as it can be, it's worth it for the puns alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T01:36:11-07:00","id":472407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=472201#post472201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just one more renown and you can do it the other way around. Pump them full of air until they're like Thunder in Big Trouble Little China.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of that, now I'm wondering if one can make lightning/electricity with this gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T03:24:39-07:00","id":472469,"title":"","content":"I'd say you'd manage a lightning storm using a catastrophic Control Air at the very least. Small scale, it's a bit murkier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T05:10:53-07:00","id":472534,"title":"","content":"With the right fetish, sure, since they now allow you to alter existing gifts you could probably manage Influence of anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T07:04:23-07:00","id":472670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=472534#post472534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the right fetish, sure, since they now allow you to alter existing gifts you could probably manage Influence of anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in that case, a combination of a Fetish with a Blood Spirit, and Influence Water, you can drain them dry of blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T07:26:18-07:00","id":472675,"title":"","content":"That would be a good way to do it, though it would need to be designed to specifically affect that gift and not just any fetish with a blood spirit. I think you'd need an exceptional success unless they were already bleeding from an open wound, but sure.<br /> <br /> You wouldn't even need the Elemental Gifts. You could just get a fetish that flat out does Influences like the Storm Coil. But you'd likely have a larger dice pool basing it off the gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-08-2015, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:04:48-07:00","id":472886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=472469#post472469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say you'd manage a lightning storm using a catastrophic Control Air at the very least. Small scale, it's a bit murkier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, with the caveat that while you can make a thunder storm with Influence: Air, you can't direct the Lightning without Influence: Lightning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:07:44-07:00","id":472978,"title":"","content":"Since we have people who seem to have a firer grasp on Influence than I - what level would a Computer spirit need to, you know, access and use a computer (sayunder threat by an Uratha?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:17:59-07:00","id":473000,"title":"","content":"I mean, it depends on what you want to do with the computer. Improve its processing speed? That'd be Strengthen (1 dot). Change some settings? Manipulate (2 dots). Make it do weird shit? Control (3 dots). Make a new computer? Create (4 dots). Make a lot of new computers? Mass Create (5 dots).<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'd say anything you could accomplish by interfacing with the computer normally (change brightness, surf the net, make a spreadsheet, etc.) would be covered under Manipulate. Control would be to make it do things it's not meant to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-08-2015, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:23:49-07:00","id":473004,"title":"","content":"That wouldn't actually involve Influence, you'd just bring a computer spirit over and order it to manifest and use a computer.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, it could use its influences to enhance the computer abilities of someone using a computer, manipulate a computer so that it's able to do things it probably could have done before but easier, or just outright control it so it could do whatever it wanted, within reason.<br /> <br /> Influence is five powers, and they all do what their names suggest.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Strengthen - Enhances its Sphere of Influence<br /> \u2022\u2022 Manipulate - Minor changes within Sphere of Influence<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Control - Dramatic changes within Sphere of Influence<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Create - Create a new example of its Sphere of Influence<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Mass Create - Create many new examples of its Sphere of Influence<br /> <br /> By default these changes are temporary, but can be made to last longer or be permanent if a spirit has enough Influence and spends the essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:28:32-07:00","id":473008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=472978#post472978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we have people who seem to have a firer grasp on Influence than I - what level would a Computer spirit need to, you know, access and use a computer (sayunder threat by an Uratha?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that Strengthen can let the computer do something better that it is already doing (or just generally run faster, more efficiently, etc.).<br /> <br /> Manipulate can make the computer do anything it can naturally do (so if there would be a way to access the data using the available software and hardware, the spirit can do it at this level). So I'd say access and use would normally be at this level, barring extremely stringent security measures.<br /> <br /> Control can make the computer do anything, even if the software would not be readily available or the hardware is lacking, as long as it is something a hypothetical computer could do. Here security isn't really a problem anymore, as the spirit has total control over everything the computer does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:29:01-07:00","id":473009,"title":"","content":"The computer example is interesting given the 5-dot Veil Rite that calls on lots of minor spirits to seek out and garble examples of a certain phenomenon. At what point could a spirit use its influence to corrupt data? Specifically permanently? Would they just need to Maninpulate the saved data bits in a random fashion so that the record is junk, and having done so relinquish control and let the bits naturally stay where they were put?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:29:46-07:00","id":473010,"title":"","content":"Probably just Manipulate, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:31:58-07:00","id":473014,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that sounds like Manipulate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T13:14:55-07:00","id":476228,"title":"","content":"The catastropic facet it\u00b4s something marvelous. <br /> <br /> With 10 miles radius, it\u00b4s possible to destroy a city. Maybe the New Orleans Hurricane was some pissed werewolf after all.<br /> <br /> The cost it\u00b4s gigantic, but the effect it\u00b4s far from imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5595-prelks","name":"Prelks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T06:50:26-07:00","id":476879,"title":"","content":"Being as Strengthen is speicifically called out as adding Structure and Durability, I'm thinking a 1-dot effect of Heart of Water could be a Path of Frost style power where you freeze water enough to run on it. With four dots and the ability to spend 5 Essence per turn, you could probably do Iceman style ice-path creation (Create and the Strengthen[freeze] all at once).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T09:12:46-07:00","id":477044,"title":"","content":"I was thinking you could ramp up the surface tension a bit and full-on pull a Jesus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T09:49:57-07:00","id":477059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=476879#post476879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being as Strengthen is speicifically called out as adding Structure and Durability, I'm thinking a 1-dot effect of Heart of Water could be a Path of Frost style power where you freeze water enough to run on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's pretty clear that that's talking about things that <i>have</i> Structure and Durability, seeing as the alternative is being able to literally run on anger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T10:26:23-07:00","id":477073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=477059#post477059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's pretty clear that that's talking about things that <i>have</i> Structure and Durability, seeing as the alternative is being able to literally run on anger.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a completely unreasonable arguement, but it extrapolates things a little too far. Water has a physical location and anger doesn't. And there's Elfive's semi-jocular point that surface tension is a real phenomenon that some animals do exploit to run on water. And water does become solid naturally at times, whereas emotions don't.<br /> <br /> Edit: thinking about it a little bit more, your suggestion would make a badass Fetish, since they offer and warp Gifts and influences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T10:36:46-07:00","id":477078,"title":"","content":"I agree with Satchel. Changing water from liquid to solid would be at least Manipulate, maybe Control for the most dramatic displays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T11:04:27-07:00","id":477093,"title":"","content":"With most materials I would agree that changing states of matter would require Control. But water is somewhat of a special case, since it exists naturally in liquid, solid, and gas forms on earth. If you can change the temperature of water with Manipulate, you can definitely change its state. I'd also allow a character to change water vapor to liquid water or liquid water to ice with Strengthen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T11:16:11-07:00","id":477104,"title":"","content":"I can see Manipulate being a reasonable stipulation, but Strengthen doesn't seem to me like a stretch for this case. I think it might be a place where one should discuss it with their ST if they plan to make use of this influence in this way.<br /> <br /> Being able to run on water also opens up the possibility of removing (at least partially) the drawback of that HiD Rite that lets your run places super fast so long as you wouldn't have to cross water to get there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T11:19:27-07:00","id":477105,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd definitely require Control to raise the surface tension of water enough to support a human body without actually changing it to ice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T05:59:42-07:00","id":477856,"title":"","content":"That's reasonable based on the &quot;Control is for distinctly unnatural effects&quot; idiom. It does lead to the unfortunate situation where we have good justifiactions to require 1, 2, and 3 dots and Essence for what is more or less the exact same effect. The surface tention thing is a little less conspicuous than the freezing, but still.<br /> Thinking through it again, though, Strengthen can be a pretty unnatural thing. Maybe it's less overt than the levitation offered by Control, but making you could use Influence(Glass) to make a wine glass withstand bullets. And water does have structure and durability when it's not melted, so one could argue that it has those things, just at 0 when it's liquid water. In that case the &quot;Adding Sructure and Durability only works on things that already have Structure and Durability&quot; arguement stops holding up, or at least stops being a restriction.<br /> <br /> Edit: Looking back at the text for Strengthen, it doesn't add Durability, just Structure, and it gives dots based on the Rank of whoever is using it. Hmm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":". 04-12-2015, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T07:40:08-07:00","id":477912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=477856#post477856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's reasonable based on the &amp;quot;Control is for distinctly unnatural effects&amp;quot; idiom. It does lead to the unfortunate situation where we have good justifiactions to require 1, 2, and 3 dots and Essence for what is more or less the exact same effect. The surface tention thing is a little less conspicuous than the freezing, but still.<br /> Thinking through it again, though, Strengthen can be a pretty unnatural thing. Maybe it's less overt than the levitation offered by Control, but making you could use Influence(Glass) to make a wine glass withstand bullets. And water does have structure and durability when it's not melted, so one could argue that it has those things, just at 0 when it's liquid water. In that case the &amp;quot;Adding Sructure and Durability only works on things that already have Structure and Durability&amp;quot; arguement stops holding up, or at least stops being a restriction.<br /> <br /> Edit: Looking back at the text for Strengthen, it doesn't add Durability, just Structure, and it gives dots based on the Rank of whoever is using it. Hmm...</div> </div> </div> </div>By that logic though, you could use Strengthen to add Durability to any matter at all, since all matter can exist as solid, liquid, gas, or plasma at the right temperature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T10:46:07-07:00","id":478107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=477912#post477912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By that logic though, you could use Strengthen to add Durability to any matter at all, since all matter can exist as solid, liquid, gas, or plasma at the right temperature.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Largely, yes. But some elements also require certain non-standard pressures to achieve those other states. Then again, it's magic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T10:56:10-07:00","id":478114,"title":"","content":"Yes, but Influence is a specific kind of magic that plays up the natural properties of an existing concept, emotion, animal or plant or element or anything. Fire doesn't really have a property of being hard or solid to begin with, so why would Strengthening Fire make a solid fire? You get the same dilemma with air. Water offers an argument due to surface tension, but that is just as much a property of air as it is of water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T11:09:45-07:00","id":478126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478114#post478114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but Influence is a specific kind of magic that plays up the natural properties of an existing concept, emotion, animal or plant or element or anything. Fire doesn't really have a property of being hard or solid to begin with, so why would Strengthening Fire make a solid fire? You get the same dilemma with air. Water offers an argument due to surface tension, but that is just as much a property of air as it is of water.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well fire isn't matter, so it's not the best analogy. But yeah, Strengthen shouldn't be able to make non-solid Mater viscous enough to support any significant amount of weight, let alone give it a positive Durability rating. Strengthen just enhances an Influence's natural properties, it doesn't make it do things it couldn't naturally do. Likewise, Manipulate alters an Influence within the constraints of its natural properties. It just happens that the conditions on earth are such that water locally has very versatile natural properties. But any changes that go beyond those constraints (such as making it effectly solid without freezing it) would require Control.<br /> <br /> Although, this conversation has lead me to the conclusion that freezing water probably would require Manipulate, not Strengthen. So there's definitely value in this kind of exploration of the possibilities of Influences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T11:30:53-07:00","id":478141,"title":"","content":"I don't know if Influence: Water would be able to freeze. I'd probably rule against it in my own games, since that would be the purview of Influence: Ice. But I don't think it's something everyone should stick to.<br /> <br /> I just like how with Catastrophe you can make some of Syfy's greatest natural disaster movies come to life. <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt2494032/?ref_=fn_al_tt_1\" target=\"_blank\">Stonados </a>and <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt3969972/?ref_=fn_al_tt_1\" target=\"_blank\">firequakes</a>, then with just a fetish you can have your <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt2724064/?ref_=nv_sr_1\" target=\"_blank\">sharknados</a> and <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt2622826/?ref_=nv_sr_2\" target=\"_blank\">avalanche sharks</a> and <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1334456/?ref_=tt_rec_tt\" target=\"_blank\">ice twisters</a> and <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0840304/?ref_=fn_al_tt_2\" target=\"_blank\">ice spiders</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T11:35:34-07:00","id":478146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478141#post478141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if Influence: Water would be able to freeze. I'd probably rule against it in my own games, since that would be the purview of Influence: Ice. But I don't think it's something everyone should stick to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you allow Influence: Earth to create a volcano (or cause an existing one to errupt)? Because if Water and Ice are separate Influences, so should Earth and Magma be.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm ok with some overlap between influences. With the water example, I would allow Influence: Water to affect water ice, but not carbon dioxide ice (commonly known as &quot;dry ice&quot;). Likewise, I would allow Influence: Ice to affect water ice or carbon dioxide ice, but not liquid water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-12-2015, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T11:51:49-07:00","id":478152,"title":"","content":"An existing one could be triggered to erupt by movements of the earth, just like you could create a flood by using earth to destroy a dam. But I don't think you could use earth to just create a new volcano from scratch, no.<br /> <br /> I understand what you're saying, but as I see it spirits aren't based off of that kind of logic, you know? A greed spirit isn't necessarily going to have any control over money, but greed could be used to get money. Fire influence could be used to expand a fire, and make a lot of smoke, but it couldn't control the smoke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T12:07:53-07:00","id":478162,"title":"","content":"I think it depends on the spirit. The spirit of a lake in a particularly cold region might be able to freeze the surface of it without influence: ice because that's just how lakes work where it lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T12:11:01-07:00","id":478166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478152#post478152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An existing one could be triggered to erupt by movements of the earth, just like you could create a flood by using earth to destroy a dam. But I don't think you could use earth to just create a new volcano from scratch, no.<br /> <br /> I understand what you're saying, but as I see it spirits aren't based off of that kind of logic, you know? A greed spirit isn't necessarily going to have any control over money, but greed could be used to get money. Fire influence could be used to expand a fire, and make a lot of smoke, but it couldn't control the smoke.</div> </div> </div> </div>But money isn't greed and smoke isn't fire. Ice is literally cold water (or, water ice is, anyway) and magma is literally hot rock. I just don't think temperature change would remove a substance from a spirit's sphere of influence. It also gets a little hairy to start excluding certain abilities from an influence on the grounds that it's covered by a different influence. Like, can Influence: cars not be used to make a car go really fast because that's the purview of Influence: speed? Can it not be used to turn the car on because that's the purview of Influence: machines? Can it not change the car's shape because that's the purview of Influence: metal? Like, the subjectivity of Influences makes overlap inherently unavoidable. I think as long as each influence has a unique combination of things it can do, it doesn't matter if some of those things can also be done by other influences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T12:12:12-07:00","id":478167,"title":"","content":"Or the spirit of the lake might get diminished, as Winter spirits bring ice spirits to sit on top of it.<br /> <br /> But, that's a spirit of a specific lake. It would probably have Influence: Lakes, and likely not be able to make it rain, drain the water from people, or make your swimming pool drown you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T12:22:44-07:00","id":478198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478166#post478166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ice is literally cold water (or, water ice is, anyway) and magma is literally hot rock. I just don't think temperature change would remove a substance from a spirit's sphere of influence. It also gets a little hairy to start excluding certain abilities from an influence on the grounds that it's covered by a different influence. Like, can Influence: cars not be used to make a car go really fast because that's the purview of Influence: speed? Can it not be used to turn the car on because that's the purview of Influence: machines? Can it not change the car's shape because that's the purview of Influence: metal? Like, the subjectivity of Influences makes overlap inherently unavoidable. I think as long as each influence has a unique combination of things it can do, it doesn't matter if some of those things can also be done by other influences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ice is frozen water. Conceptually there's a difference. Most people on Earth wouldn't look at an iceberg or an ice cube and naturally think, 'frozen water,' despite them knowing what it is. Cars, conceptually, can go fast, can turn on and off, they're natural states of cars. Cars could also be crushed into metal cubes or divided up into plastic and metal parts, at which point it wouldn't be a car. Water to ice is a drastic change, and from the memories and feelings of everything that makes spirits, it has very little similarity to water.<br /> <br /> At that point, Water could control steam and clouds, Earth could control particulate in the air, such as Smoke. A newspaper is just pulped wood, wood is just a tree, would a tree spirit be able to tell you how your stocks are doing? Money is often made from plant fibers and ink, would you let Influence: Plants create money?<br /> <br /> 'This Facet grants power over wave and water, over rain and river. At the Uratha\u2019s call, it surges, strengthens or recedes.'<br /> <br /> I wouldn't allow it, but I wouldn't try to convince anyone else from allowing it at their table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-12-2015, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T14:10:01-07:00","id":478293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478198#post478198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ice is frozen water. Conceptually there's a difference. Most people on Earth wouldn't look at an iceberg or an ice cube and naturally think, 'frozen water,' despite them knowing what it is. Cars, conceptually, can go fast, can turn on and off, they're natural states of cars. Cars could also be crushed into metal cubes or divided up into plastic and metal parts, at which point it wouldn't be a car. Water to ice is a drastic change, and from the memories and feelings of everything that makes spirits, it has very little similarity to water.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see where you're coming from, I just disagree on the conceptual differences between different states of the same material. I mean, most media that involves control over elements, ice and sometimes steam are included under the umbrella of water, so obviously there's prescedent for pop cultural perception of frozen water as conceptually included in water.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478198#post478198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At that point, Water could control steam and clouds, Earth could control particulate in the air, such as Smoke. A newspaper is just pulped wood, wood is just a tree, would a tree spirit be able to tell you how your stocks are doing? Money is often made from plant fibers and ink, would you let Influence: Plants create money?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd definitely allow influence: water to affect water vapor (and therefore clouds and rain/snow), and for influence: earth to affect dirt particles in the air. I'm a little iffy on influence: trees making paper because there's a lot more processing involved than just pulping the wood, and at that point it's not the same material. Maybe with influence: wood and an extend action? I don't know enough about how paper is made to be confident in such a ruling. Certainly not paper bills, because they also require ink, and a lot of other stuff not found in trees. I would, however allow influence: metal to make coins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478198#post478198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'This Facet grants power over wave and water, over rain and river. At the Uratha\u2019s call, it surges, strengthens or recedes.'</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're using that description as hard limitations on what can be done with Influence: water, it's not going to be able to do much. Note though, that rain is included, which implies you can make rain, which requires controlling clouds, i.e. water vapor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478198#post478198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't allow it, but I wouldn't try to convince anyone else from allowing it at their table.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure, and I don't mean to sound like I'm trying to convince you to allow it at your table. As I mentioned earlier, I find value in simply exploring the possibilities of an Influence. My opinion has already shifted once over the course of this discussion (in regards to what level of Influence I would call for to freeze water), so I'm more here to help refine my own opinion than to try to change that of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T15:04:30-07:00","id":478339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478293#post478293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see where you're coming from, I just disagree on the conceptual differences between different states of the same material. I mean, most media that involves control over elements, ice and sometimes steam are included under the umbrella of water, so obviously there's prescedent for pop cultural perception of frozen water as conceptually included in water.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of them probably don't use the same concept of the spirit plane as World of Darkness does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd definitely allow influence: water to affect water vapor (and therefore clouds and rain/snow), and for influence: earth to affect dirt particles in the air. I'm a little iffy on influence: trees making paper because there's a lot more processing involved than just pulping the wood, and at that point it's not the same material. Maybe with influence: wood and an extend action? I don't know enough about how paper is made to be confident in such a ruling. Certainly not paper bills, because they also require ink, and a lot of other stuff not found in trees. I would, however allow influence: metal to make coins. </div> </div> </div>Why just Influence: Metal and not Earth? Earth doesn't specifically state dirt or soil. It's the element of Earth, with rock and ore. And wouldn't Influence: Air let you create dry ice?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're using that description as hard limitations on what can be done with Influence: water, it's not going to be able to do much. Note though, that rain is included, which implies you can make rain, which requires controlling clouds, i.e. water vapor. </div> </div> </div>Not really, the Create ability of Influence doesn't seem to pull things from other places, it seems to create it out of nothing, so you wouldn't require a cloud.<br /> <br /> I'd only have it available through a fetish that altered the gift or another gift entirely. Or you could use Hunt of Fire and Ice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T15:34:06-07:00","id":478369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478339#post478339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of them probably don't use the same concept of the spirit plane as World of Darkness does.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't, but they are evidence that the general population's concept of the relationship between ice and water is linked. If the concept is what matters (and I do agree that it is), I think it's relevant that enough people conceptualize water and ice as the same thing that Avatar's water benders can also control ice, ninjas with water powers in Naruto can also control ice, Mercury adepts in Golden Sun learn ice spells even with only Mercury Djinni set, and a significant portion of Ice type Pokemon are also part water (though the fact that they're separate types at all in Pokemon might actually be a counter-example). Modern understanding of the states of matter, as well as pop culture, have affected the general perception of the relationship between ice and water to the point where I believe they are conceptually similar enough to be affected by the same Influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478339#post478339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why just Influence: Metal and not Earth? Earth doesn't specifically state dirt or soil. It's the element of Earth, with rock and ore. And wouldn't Influence: Air let you create dry ice?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say just metal and not earth. To make coins out of thin air with Influence: earth? Eh, I don't see Create as allowing quite that much specificity, but I would certainly allow you to create the raw materials with it, and then to shape them into coins with Control. Or to melt them down with Manipulate and then mint them the old fashioned way. Dry Ice typically refers to frozen carbon dioxide. Air on earth is made primarily out of Nitrogen, and solid nitrogen doesn't typically occur on earth outside of controlled laboratory conditions. I would allow nitrogen ice to be created with four dots of influence: ice, and I would allow the nitrogen in the air to be turned to ice with three dots of influence: ice, air, or cold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478339#post478339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, the Create ability of Influence doesn't seem to pull things from other places, it seems to create it out of nothing, so you wouldn't require a cloud.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, I was assuming use of Manipulate or Control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478339#post478339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd only have it available through a fetish that altered the gift or another gift entirely. Or you could use Hunt of Fire and Ice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I'd of course agree to your ruling at your table, though I would rule differently at mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T15:45:35-07:00","id":478380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478369#post478369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't, but they are evidence that the general population's concept of the relationship between ice and water is linked. If the concept is what matters (and I do agree that it is), I think it's relevant that enough people conceptualize water and ice as the same thing that Avatar's water benders can also control ice, ninjas with water powers in Naruto can also control ice, Mercury adepts in Golden Sun learn ice spells even with only Mercury Djinni set, and a significant portion of Ice type Pokemon are also part water (though the fact that they're separate types at all in Pokemon might actually be a counter-example). Modern understanding of the states of matter, as well as pop culture, have affected the general perception of the relationship between ice and water to the point where I believe they are conceptually similar enough to be affected by the same Influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd call this a false equivalence, given that the examples you're comparing are specifically subdivided into a set of discrete elements that other phenomena are fitted into; the <i>Hisil</i> approaches this from the opposite direction by making spirits of similar concepts sympathetically related or at loosely affiliated with each other when they interact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T16:11:34-07:00","id":478404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478380#post478380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd call this a false equivalence, given that the examples you're comparing are specifically subdivided into a set of discrete elements that other phenomena are fitted into; the <i>Hisil</i> approaches this from the opposite direction by making spirits of similar concepts sympathetically related or at loosely affiliated with each other when they interact.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, I hadn't considered that. Thanka for catching it. But would you say there is no overlap in the capabilities of different influences? Like, frosting up the windows on a humid day. Influence: cold, ice, water, weather, what? I would say all of the above. I guess it's just a question of where you do or do not allow overlap, and personally, I'm more confortable with more overlap than less, since any line you draw is going to be arbitrary anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T01:25:45-07:00","id":478871,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd be willing to let werewolves be a bit more liberal with their influences than spirits. Benefits of a flexible human mindset.<br /> <br /> A spirit of water can't control blood or ice, because it's nature doesn't allow it to recognise them as the same thing. An uratha who has any knowledge of science knows better. As far as spirits would see it, they can <i>cheat. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T04:43:47-07:00","id":478950,"title":"","content":"As a physics aside, there's no such thing as nitrogen ice or carbon dioxide ice. The word ice only refers to water in its solid form. <br /> <br /> Influence ice should affect only frozen h2o. <br /> Influence air should not be able to make solid co2. <br /> <br /> Conceptually and physically these are different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","user":"FlailBot","date":". 04-13-2015, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T05:04:45-07:00","id":478961,"title":"","content":"Physics is the one place ice <i>doesn't </i>mean just water ice. It's a fairly common term for anything volatile that melts above 100 Kelvin. Solid carbon dioxide is commonly called &quot;dry ice&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T07:56:31-07:00","id":479040,"title":"","content":"I'd like to throw my hat back in here.<br /> Given that Strengthen doesn't add Durability (as I had mistakenly thought based on an early reading), it makes sense that it can't be used to make things that are typically non-solid things solid. I think this much has been established.<br /> <br /> Manipulate can be used to change the temperature of a thing. Charlaquin (and possibly others, but his/her assertions are the only ones I remember at the moment) has been saying this for a while and I don't recall seeing anyone dispute that general claim. As such, if something can be frozen through a change in temperature, Manipulate can freeze it.<br /> <br /> As to the question of overlaps in Influence, I would point to the difference between an Umia and Ilthum, given that those are basic spirit distinctions. Umia take the form of broad categories of things (Water, Air, Information, Mamals, Emotions, etc.) whereas Ilthum are the sub-groups of spirits within those that cling to more specific phenomena (Rain, Wind, Books, Wolves, Fear, etc.) The thing is, Ilthum are not a natural spirit division - they pick those and latch onto them to speed their growth. As such, something like Ice would be a sub-set of Water. Maybe it's power could leak out to beyond the bounds of Water when faced with frozen things that are not water, but when dealing with water, anything Influence: Ice could do, Influence: Water could do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T12:57:46-07:00","id":479367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts?p=478961#post478961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physics is the one place ice <i>doesn't </i>mean just water ice. It's a fairly common term for anything volatile that melts above 100 Kelvin. Solid carbon dioxide is commonly called &quot;dry ice&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from dry ice, which a colloquial term, I can think of nothing else I would refer to as ice. I might say, frozen X or solid Y, but never e.g. &quot;oh yeah, that's gallium ice.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the argument that concepts are important, not minor corner cases of interpretation (like solid CO2 falling under Air). Air conjures up non-technical ideas about wind, storms, breathing, swirling leaves, etc. Spirits are highly tied to ideas and concepts and I think we're doing ourselves no favors by looking with such a critical eye at these things.<br /> <br /> As for travelling on water, I think manipulate is enough, just &quot;create&quot; a jet under yourself that's constantly flowing upwards. No need to mess with the surface tension or trample into Ice territory. :-) Note: This is playful, I do think that there is some overlap between influences.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}